@@ -3,3 +3,12 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of a parsed JSON
+document that a JSON Pointer refers to (`""` is the whole document, `"/foo/0"` the first element of
+`foo`). It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not valid per RFC 6901, or when it does not resolve to
+a value of the document: missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index (`01`), `-` (the
+nonexistent element past the end of an array), or a step through a primitive. Only own members are
+resolved, so `/constructor` or `/foo/length` never reach inherited properties.
